# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/spell_sources.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event evo_first_flame
# en: Flame, Properly
title [1ee0a5] = 火焰，正式的
# en: {level(evocation) == 0: Professor Thorne writes one word on the board: FLAME. "Every duellist you will ever face has this ready before their wand is out," he says. "So will you. By Friday."|{level(evocation) == 1: Evocation II meets at the duel hall, not the lectern. Thorne has set a straw target forty paces off. "Last year you lit candles. This year the fire goes where you send it, and arrives."|Advanced Evocation opens with Thorne standing in a ring of fire he did not light. "This is what a duel looks like when it goes wrong," he says. "Your flame must hold while you are hit." He has hired a senior to hit you.}}
text [d12e8e] = {level(evocation) == 0: 索恩教授在黑板上写下一个词：火焰。“你们将来遇到的每个决斗者，魔杖还没拔出来就已经备好了这个，”他说，“你们也会。周五之前。”|{level(evocation) == 1: 塑能术 II 不在讲台前上，而在决斗厅。索恩在四十步外立了一个草靶。“去年你们点蜡烛。今年，火要去你让它去的地方，并且到达。”|高等塑能术的第一课，索恩站在一圈不是他点的火里。“决斗出岔子时就是这个样子，”他说，“你的火焰在挨打时也必须不灭。”他雇了一个高年级生来打你。}}
# en: A lecture hall with one word chalked on the board, students holding small flames on their palms, a grey-bearded professor watching from the lectern.
scene [756ae5] = 一间讲堂，黑板上用粉笔写着一个词，学生们掌心托着小小的火焰，一位灰胡子教授在讲台上看着。
# en: Drill it until it comes
opt.left.label [0dbd59] = 练到它听话为止
# en: {level(evocation) == 0: By Friday the flame comes when you call it, and your fingertips are pink and tender. Thorne looks at your palm for a long moment. "Hm," he says.|{level(evocation) == 1: You throw until your sleeves smoke. On the sixtieth try the straw target goes up with a satisfying whump. Thorne writes something down, without comment.|The senior hits you nine times. On the tenth your flame stays lit through it, and the senior, singed, asks for a rest. Thorne says "Better," which is new.}}
opt.left.say.1 [ea1481] = {level(evocation) == 0: 到周五，火焰一唤就来，你的指尖又红又嫩。索恩盯着你的手掌看了很久。“嗯，”他说。|{level(evocation) == 1: 你扔到袖子冒烟。第六十次，草靶轰地烧了起来，听着真痛快。索恩记下了什么，不置一词。|那个高年级生打了你九下。第十下时你的火焰撑住了没灭，被燎了一下的高年级生要求歇会儿。索恩说了声“好些了”，这是头一回。}}
# en: Learn the shape of it first
opt.right.label [4ff4f7] = 先摸清它的形状
# en: {level(evocation) == 0: You work it out on paper while the room fills with small fires. Yours comes last, on Thursday night, alone in your room. It's a very correct flame.|{level(evocation) == 1: You chart the target's distance and the arc a flame takes. Your fire lands late but dead centre. Nobody saw, because they'd gone to lunch.|You watch how Thorne's ring keeps burning when the senior hits him. It takes a week of evenings to copy it, and the class teases you for every one.}}
opt.right.say.1 [c7a379] = {level(evocation) == 0: 满屋子都是小火苗的时候，你还在纸上推演。你的火最后才来，在周四夜里，你一个人在房间里。那是一团非常标准的火焰。|{level(evocation) == 1: 你算出靶子的距离和火焰飞行的弧线。你的火来得晚，却正中靶心。没人看见，大家都去吃午饭了。|你观察索恩那圈火在被击中时如何不灭。花了一周的晚上才学到手，全班每晚都在笑话你。}}

@event astro_first_foresight
# en: A Moment Ahead
title [bcae99] = 提前一刻
# en: {level(astromancy) == 0: Astromancy I begins with a coin. The lecturer spins it on the brass desk and asks which way it will fall. "Don't guess," the lecturer says. "Look a moment ahead and read it."|{level(astromancy) == 1: Astromancy II, and Foresight must reach further. The lecturer deals star cards face down. "The next three, in order, before I turn them."|Advanced Astromancy: the lecturer sits opposite you and says nothing at all. "Foresee what I am about to say," the lecturer says at last, "and say it first."}}
text [904f55] = {level(astromancy) == 0: 星象 I 从一枚硬币开始。讲师在黄铜桌上转起硬币，问它会落成哪面。“别猜，”讲师说，“往前看一刻，读出来。”|{level(astromancy) == 1: 星象 II，预见必须看得更远。讲师把星牌背面朝上发下来。“接下来三张，按顺序，在我翻开之前说出来。”|高等星象：讲师坐在你对面，一言不发。“预见我要说的话，”讲师终于开口，“然后抢先说出来。”}}
# en: An observatory classroom by day, a coin spinning on a brass desk, students leaning in with their eyes half-closed.
scene [175cf7] = 白天的观星台教室，一枚硬币在黄铜桌上旋转，学生们半眯着眼凑过去。
# en: Look ahead until you see it
opt.left.label [8b5160] = 往前看直到看见
# en: {level(astromancy) == 0: The coin falls heads eleven times before you see it fall heads first. Then you see it every time, and your head aches with how far you're leaning.|{level(astromancy) == 1: You see the third card before the first, which is the wrong order and still counts as a start. By the bell you read all three, drained to the soles of your feet.|You say "Tuesday" a heartbeat before the lecturer does. It costs you an afternoon of feeling hollowed out, and a small, rare nod.}}
opt.left.say.1 [b0e502] = {level(astromancy) == 0: 硬币落了十一次正面，你才在它落下之前看见它落成正面。之后你次次都看得见，脑袋因为往前探得太远而发疼。|{level(astromancy) == 1: 你先看见了第三张，后看见第一张，顺序错了，但也算开了个头。到下课时你三张都读出来了，累得脚底板都发空。|你比讲师早一口气说出了“星期二”。代价是一下午被掏空的感觉，外加一个难得的、小小的点头。}}
# en: Ask how far ahead to look
opt.right.label [08ab20] = 问该往前看多远
# en: {level(astromancy) == 0: "Less far than you think," says the lecturer, and makes you read the rules of it twice. You get the coin right on the last try of the hour, with the class watching.|{level(astromancy) == 1: The answer is a chart, and the chart is long. You copy it all and read the cards the next week, after everyone else.|"A breath," says the lecturer. "Anything past a breath is fortune-telling." You learn the breath slowly, and are the last in the room to get it.}}
opt.right.say.1 [9ad7b0] = {level(astromancy) == 0: “比你以为的近，”讲师说，让你把规则读了两遍。你在这节课的最后一次尝试时才猜对了硬币，全班都看着。|{level(astromancy) == 1: 答案是一张图表，图表很长。你全抄了下来，下一周才读出那几张牌，比所有人都晚。|“一口气，”讲师说，“超过一口气的就是算命了。”你慢慢学会了那一口气，是屋里最后一个学会的。}}

@event alch_first_mend
# en: The Mending Practical
title [c89d8b] = 愈合实践课
# en: {level(alchemy) == 0: Alchemy I's first practical is a cracked teacup on every bench. Sister Amaranth sets them down without looking up. "Mend it," she says. "Then I'll let you near a person."|{level(alchemy) == 1: Alchemy II moves into the infirmary. Sister Amaranth hands you a first-year with a split lip from the Duelling Circle. "Skin this time," she says. "It argues more than china."|Advanced Alchemy: Mend for what's deep. Sister Amaranth gives you a sprained wrist, its unhappy owner and her own pocket watch. "Bone takes patience," she says. "Patients don't."}}
text [450246] = {level(alchemy) == 0: 炼金 I 的第一堂实践课，每张实验台上都放着一只裂了的茶杯。阿玛兰斯修女头也不抬地摆好。“把它补好，”她说，“补好了，我才让你们给活人治伤。”|{level(alchemy) == 1: 炼金 II 搬进了医务室。阿玛兰斯修女交给你一个在决斗社磕破了嘴唇的新生。“这回是皮肉，”她说，“比瓷器爱顶嘴。”|高等炼金：治深处的伤。阿玛兰斯修女给了你一只扭伤的手腕、手腕那位不高兴的主人，还有她自己的怀表。“骨头需要耐心，”她说，“病人可没有。”}}
# en: An alchemy bench with a row of cracked teacups, a healer setting down the last one, students holding their hands above them.
scene [309cce] = 一张炼金实验台上摆着一排裂了的茶杯，一位医师放下最后一只，学生们把手悬在杯子上方。
# en: Mend it until it holds
opt.left.label [8a7bb1] = 补到它撑得住
# en: {level(alchemy) == 0: Your cup holds tea on the fifth try and leaks on the sixth, and you've spent everything getting there. Sister Amaranth pours some anyway and drinks it. "Keep doing that," she says.|{level(alchemy) == 1: The lip closes under your hand, slowly, and you feel every bit of it leave you. The first-year says it tickles. Sister Amaranth says that means it worked.|The sprain knits with the watch ticking beside you. You're wrung out by the end, and the wrist bends like a wrist. Sister Amaranth puts the watch away. "Again tomorrow," she says, which is praise.}}
opt.left.say.1 [750ddd] = {level(alchemy) == 0: 你的茶杯第五次能盛住茶，第六次又漏了，你为此耗光了力气。阿玛兰斯修女还是倒了茶喝了。“保持住，”她说。|{level(alchemy) == 1: 嘴唇在你手下慢慢合上，你感觉到每一分都从你身上流走。新生说有点痒。阿玛兰斯修女说那就是成了。|扭伤在怀表的滴答声里愈合。到最后你精疲力竭，那只手腕弯起来就是一只手腕。阿玛兰斯修女收起怀表。“明天再来，”她说，这是夸奖。}}
# en: Watch her do one first
opt.right.label [8e2d6e] = 先看她做一遍
# en: {level(alchemy) == 0: She mends hers without stopping her conversation with the next bench. You copy her hands. Yours takes the whole hour, and the bench beside you finishes first.|{level(alchemy) == 1: You watch her close a cut from the inside out. When your turn comes it's slower than hers by a mile, and the first-year sighs the whole time.|You watch her set a wrist and mend it in one quiet minute. Yours takes twenty, and the patient tells you about every one.}}
opt.right.say.1 [e8a595] = {level(alchemy) == 0: 她一边补自己的杯子，一边照旧和邻桌的人聊着天。你模仿她的手法。你的那只用了一整节课，邻桌的同学都比你先补好了。|{level(alchemy) == 1: 你看她由里向外合上一道伤口。轮到你时，比她慢了一大截，那个新生一直在叹气。|你看她用安静的一分钟接好并治好一只手腕。你的用了二十分钟，病人把每一分钟都讲给你听。}}

@event illu_first_glamour
# en: Lighting, Not Lying
title [9ae47b] = 是打光，不是撒谎
# en: {level(illusion) == 0: Illusion I begins where Professor Vey always begins: every student glamours their own face first, one small change held for a minute. Then she sits on her desk. "Now make me like you more, without a word. Glamour is not lying. It's lighting."|{level(illusion) == 1: Illusion II: glamour that lasts past the door. Vey sends you to the refectory at lunch with one rule. "Be remembered for something you didn't do."|Advanced Illusion opens with Vey wearing your face. She teaches the first ten minutes in your voice, quite well. "Now take it back," she says.}}
text [d976e0] = {level(illusion) == 0: 幻术 I 的开头和维伊教授每次一样：每个学生先给自己的脸施魅影，做一处小小的改变，维持一分钟。然后她坐到讲桌上。“现在一句话也不说，让我更喜欢你们。魅影不是撒谎，是打光。”|{level(illusion) == 1: 幻术 II：出了门还不散的魅影。维伊让你午饭时去膳堂，只有一条规矩：“让人记住你没做过的一件事。”|高等幻术第一课，维伊顶着你的脸。她用你的声音讲了前十分钟，讲得还挺好。“现在把它拿回去，”她说。}}
# en: A bright classroom where a smiling professor in a violet scarf sits on her own desk, students across from her trying very hard to look likeable.
scene [9ff3bc] = 一间明亮的教室，一位围着紫色围巾、面带微笑的教授坐在自己的讲桌上，对面的学生们拼命想显得讨人喜欢。
# en: Try it on Vey herself
opt.left.label [08df65] = 直接对维伊试
# en: {level(illusion) == 0: Vey likes you a great deal for almost a minute, then shakes it off and applauds. You feel wrung out, as if you'd smiled all day.|{level(illusion) == 1: By supper three people remember you saving the cook from a falling ladle. There was no ladle. You're too tired to enjoy it.|You take your face back from her a feature at a time. It costs you everything you had. Vey hands over the last one, your frown, with regret.}}
opt.left.say.1 [9392fc] = {level(illusion) == 0: 维伊非常喜欢了你将近一分钟，然后甩开了它，鼓起掌来。你累得像笑了一整天。|{level(illusion) == 1: 到晚饭时，有三个人记得你从掉落的长柄勺下救了厨师。根本没有什么勺子。你累得高兴不起来。|你一个五官一个五官地把脸从她那儿拿回来。这用光了你所有的力气。维伊把最后一样——你的皱眉——依依不舍地还给了你。}}
# en: Practise on a mirror first
opt.right.label [380b83] = 先对着镜子练
# en: {level(illusion) == 0: You glamour your reflection, which likes you and is no help at all. Vey catches you at it. "Start with a harder audience," she says, and the class laughs.|{level(illusion) == 1: You rehearse in the washroom mirror until a prefect walks in on you being charming at nobody. The glamour works on the second day.|You practise your own face for a week before you try to take it back. By then everyone has met Vey-as-you, and they liked her better.}}
opt.right.say.1 [82604a] = {level(illusion) == 0: 你对自己的倒影施了魅影，它很喜欢你，可一点用也没有。维伊抓到你在干这个。“找个难对付点的观众，”她说，全班都笑了。|{level(illusion) == 1: 你在盥洗室镜子前排练，直到一位级长撞见你在对着空气卖弄魅力。第二天魅影才奏效。|你对着自己的脸练了一周才去把它拿回来。到那时人人都见过“维伊版的你”，而且他们更喜欢她。}}

@event beast_first_haste
# en: Borrowed Speed
title [b659ee] = 借来的速度
# en: {level(beastcraft) == 0: Beastcraft I's first spell is taught at a run. Professor Brask points at a hare in the paddock. "Catch it. You won't, on your legs." She teaches you Haste in four words and lets the hare go.|{level(beastcraft) == 1: Beastcraft II: Haste in the air. Brask has a hawk on her glove and a broom against the fence. "Keep up with her," she says, "to the far tower and back."|Advanced Beastcraft: Brask's test is to keep pace with a hippogriff at full gallop, the length of the flight field, and still be able to talk at the end.}}
text [9701da] = {level(beastcraft) == 0: 驭兽 I 的第一道咒是跑着教的。布拉斯克教授指着围场里的一只野兔。“抓住它。靠你的腿抓不住。”她用四个词教会了你疾速，然后把野兔放了。|{level(beastcraft) == 1: 驭兽 II：空中的疾速。布拉斯克手套上停着一只鹰，篱笆边靠着一把扫帚。“跟上她，”她说，“到远塔，再回来。”|高等驭兽：布拉斯克的考验是跟一头全速奔跑的鹰头马身有翼兽并驾齐驱，跑完整个飞行场，到终点还能开口说话。}}
# en: A muddy paddock at the stables, a weathered professor pointing at a hare while a student crouches to sprint.
scene [e7a94c] = 马厩边泥泞的围场，一位饱经风霜的教授指着一只野兔，一个学生蹲下准备冲刺。
# en: Run it down
opt.left.label [69bc99] = 追上它
# en: {level(beastcraft) == 0: You catch the hare on the fourth go, briefly, and it bites you. You sleep eleven hours. Brask says that's the price, and the hare agrees.|{level(beastcraft) == 1: You reach the far tower a wingbeat behind the hawk, and the hawk looks smug about it. Your legs shake all through supper.|You run the field at the hippogriff's shoulder and say "good afternoon" at the end, gasping. Brask laughs once. You're stiff for three days.}}
opt.left.say.1 [2b8b3f] = {level(beastcraft) == 0: 第四次你抓住了野兔，抓了一小会儿，它咬了你一口。你睡了十一个小时。布拉斯克说这就是代价，野兔也同意。|{level(beastcraft) == 1: 你比鹰晚一个振翅到达远塔，鹰看起来很得意。整个晚饭你的腿都在抖。|你在鹰头马身有翼兽肩旁跑完全场，喘着气在终点说了声“下午好”。布拉斯克大笑了一声。你僵了三天。}}
# en: Study how it moves first
opt.right.label [b867e5] = 先观察它怎么移动
# en: {level(beastcraft) == 0: You watch the hare for an hour, then borrow its speed properly, once, at the end. Everyone else is already muddy and proud of it.|{level(beastcraft) == 1: You watch the hawk's turns from the fence and only fly the course at dusk, alone. It's tidy. Nobody sees.|You study the gallop from the rail until you can feel it in your knees. You run it last, slower than the rest, and very sure.}}
opt.right.say.1 [f197d8] = {level(beastcraft) == 0: 你观察了野兔一个小时，最后才好好地借来了它的速度，只一次。其他人早已满身泥巴、得意洋洋。|{level(beastcraft) == 1: 你在篱笆边看鹰怎么转弯，直到黄昏才独自飞完全程。飞得很干净。没人看见。|你在栏杆边研究它的奔跑，直到膝盖里都能感觉到。你最后一个跑，比别人慢，却非常稳。}}

@event umbral_first_shadowstep
# en: The Shadows in Between
title [d0d838] = 中间的阴影
# en: {level(umbral) == 0: Umbral Theory I. The lecturer snuffs every lamp but two and stands in the dark between them. "Shadowstep," says the voice. "In at one shadow, out at another. Don't stop in the middle."|{level(umbral) == 1: Umbral Theory II: Shadowstep under watch. The lecturer sits a prefect in the doorway with a lantern. "Out of the room," says the lecturer, "without being seen leaving it."|Advanced Umbral Theory: step, and keep stepping. At dusk the lecturer lays a path of shadows across the tower roof, chimney to chimney. "To the far side. Without the floor."}}
text [a4aaba] = {level(umbral) == 0: 暗影理论 I。讲师熄灭了除两盏以外的所有灯，站在两盏灯之间的黑暗里。“影步，”那个声音说，“从一片阴影进去，从另一片出来。别在中间停下。”|{level(umbral) == 1: 暗影理论 II：被人盯着时的影步。讲师让一位级长提着灯笼坐在门口。“出这个房间，”讲师说，“别让人看见你离开。”|高等暗影理论：迈步，接着迈步。黄昏时讲师在塔顶铺出一条阴影之路，从烟囱到烟囱。“到另一头去。别碰地面。”}}
# en: The top of the lecture tower in near darkness, two pools of lamplight on the floor and a long shadow between them, a student stepping into it.
scene [c1c385] = 讲堂塔顶几乎一片漆黑，地上两团灯光，中间一道长长的影子，一个学生正迈进去。
# en: Step through and trust it
opt.left.label [26f36a] = 迈进去，相信它
# en: {level(umbral) == 0: You step in, and the dark is cold, and you come out against a desk with your shin. It counts. The lecturer's voice says, "Again," from somewhere new.|{level(umbral) == 1: You leave by the prefect's own shadow and arrive in the corridor with your elbow in a coat rack. The prefect is still watching the door.|Chimney to chimney, six steps, and on the fifth the shadow is thinner than you thought. You land on the far side with grazed palms and a grin.}}
opt.left.say.1 [422fa6] = {level(umbral) == 0: 你迈了进去，黑暗冰冷，你出来时小腿撞上了一张桌子。这也算数。讲师的声音从某个新的方向传来：“再来。”|{level(umbral) == 1: 你从级长自己的影子里离开，出现在走廊上时胳膊肘撞进了衣帽架。级长还在盯着门。|烟囱到烟囱，六步，第五步的影子比你以为的薄。你掌心擦破，咧着嘴落在了另一头。}}
# en: Map the shadows first
opt.right.label [9d6755] = 先把阴影画下来
# en: {level(umbral) == 0: You sketch where every shadow falls before you trust one. The class has stepped twice by then and is bored of watching you. Your step, when it comes, is clean.|{level(umbral) == 1: You learn where the lantern can't reach before you move, and the bell goes first. You get out the next day, unseen and unhurried.|You chart the roof's shadows as the sun goes down and miss the light for it. You cross at full dark, alone, to no applause.}}
opt.right.say.1 [ed64e3] = {level(umbral) == 0: 你先画下每一片阴影落在哪儿，才敢信任其中一片。那时全班已经迈了两次，看你看得都腻了。你那一步迈得很干净。|{level(umbral) == 1: 你先弄清了灯笼照不到哪里才动，结果下课铃先响了。第二天你出去了，没人看见，不慌不忙。|你趁太阳落山画下塔顶的阴影，也因此错过了天光。你在全黑时独自穿过，没有掌声。}}

@event art_first_animate
# en: Make It Want One Thing
title [715246] = 只让它想要一件事
# en: Artifice begins with a broom. The lecturer says one word and the broom sweeps the workshop by itself, badly and with enthusiasm. "Animate," the lecturer says. "Give a made thing one want, and only one. Yours next."
text [2c8bb0] = 奇械术的第一课是一把扫帚。讲师说了一个词，扫帚就自己扫起了工坊，扫得很糟，热情却很高。“活化，”讲师说，“给一件造出来的东西一个念想，只给一个。下一个是你的。”
# en: A cluttered workshop with a broom sweeping the floor by itself in uneven circles, a student dodging it, brass gears on every bench.
scene [707033] = 一间杂乱的工坊，一把扫帚自己绕着不规则的圈扫地，一个学生在躲它，每张工作台上都是黄铜齿轮。
# en: Give your broom its want
opt.left.label [785d7e] = 给你的扫帚一个念想
# en: Your broom wants to sweep, and sweeps. It also wants to sweep you, and does, out of the door and halfway down the stairs. The lecturer marks it a pass.
opt.left.say.1 [44b2fc] = 你的扫帚想扫地，于是扫了起来。它也想扫你，于是把你扫出门，一路扫下了半段楼梯。讲师给了及格。
# en: Read how the old ones were made
opt.right.label [d19458] = 读读老东西是怎么造的
# en: You read the workshop's oldest notes on wanting things until your broom is the last one still lying down. When it rises, it sweeps one perfect circle and stops, satisfied.
opt.right.say.1 [8299d2] = 你翻读工坊里最老的、关于“让东西想要什么”的笔记，读到全班只剩你的扫帚还躺着。它站起来时，扫了一个完美的圆，然后满意地停下了。

@event star_first_starlight
# en: A Name to Call
title [ea00b4] = 一个可以呼唤的名字
# en: The first appointment is under the open dome, past midnight. Your tutor says a star's name aloud, the old name, the one on no chart, and points. "Ask it for a thread of its light," the tutor says. "Ask properly. It has been asked rudely before."
text [0f823e] = 第一次约课在敞开的穹顶下，过了午夜。你的导师大声说出一颗星的名字——那个古老的、没有记在任何星图上的名字——然后指向它。“向它要一缕光，”导师说，“好好要。从前有人对它很无礼。”
# en: The observatory dome open to a black sky, a tutor pointing out one faint star to a student whose hand is raised toward it.
scene [3ad912] = 观星台的穹顶向漆黑的天空敞开，一位导师向一个学生指出一颗暗淡的星，学生正朝它举起手。
# en: Call until it answers
opt.left.label [012011] = 呼唤直到它回应
# en: You call until your voice goes and your hands are numb on the rail. At four the thread comes down, no thicker than a hair, and rests in your palm, warm. You don't feel the cold again until breakfast.
opt.left.say.1 [17b053] = 你一直呼唤，直到嗓子哑了，手冻僵在栏杆上。四点钟，那缕光落了下来，不比一根头发粗，温暖地停在你掌心。直到早饭你都没再觉得冷。
# en: Learn whose name it is first
opt.right.label [45ad71] = 先弄清这是谁的名字
# en: You ask about the name instead, and get an hour of history you'll need later. The thread comes for you at dawn, the last in the dome, with the tutor already yawning.
opt.right.say.1 [6d82d4] = 你转而问起这个名字，得到了一小时你日后会用上的历史。那缕光在黎明时才来找你，你是穹顶下最后一个，导师早已哈欠连天。

@event hollow_first_seal
# en: Closed, Even to Me
title [0197ec] = 封住，连我也打不开
# en: The headmistress sets a small wooden box on the table and opens it. It is empty. "Close it," she says, "so that it stays closed. To anyone. Even to me." She sits down across from you with her hands folded. "That is Seal."
text [f8bf9e] = 院长把一只小木盒放在桌上，打开。里面是空的。“把它合上，”她说，“让它一直合着。对任何人都是。连对我也是。”她在你对面坐下，双手交叠。“这就是封缄。”
# en: A room without windows lined with black-bound books, a headmistress setting an open, empty wooden box on the table in front of a student.
scene [7d3523] = 一间没有窗户、摆满黑皮书的房间，一位院长把一只敞开的空木盒放在一个学生面前的桌上。
# en: Seal it as tight as you can
opt.left.label [e17684] = 尽全力封紧
# en: It takes everything you have and the rest of the hour. The headmistress tries the lid with one finger, then two, then not at all. "Good," she says. You feel scraped hollow until supper.
opt.left.say.1 [0017f8] = 这用掉了你所有的力气和剩下的整节课。院长用一根手指试了试盒盖，又用两根，然后不试了。“好，”她说。直到晚饭你都觉得自己被刮空了。
# en: Ask what she keeps sealed
opt.right.label [6b3304] = 问她封着些什么
# en: "Many things," she says, "for good reasons." She doesn't say more, and you seal the box with that sitting in your stomach. It holds. She doesn't try it.
opt.right.say.1 [bbf578] = “很多东西，”她说，“理由都很充分。”她没再多说，你带着这句话压在心口封上了盒子。它撑住了。她没去试。

@event lyra_teaches_wildfire
# en: Let It Run
title [a021c6] = 放它去跑
# en: Lyra lets you into the duel hall after it has closed. She cups her hands and the fire in them grows, and grows, until it lights the rafters. "They taught me to keep it small," she says. "This is what it does when I stop. {I've never shown anyone."|You've seen it once already. The offer's still open."}
text [4b1b74] = 决斗厅关门后，莱拉放你进去。她捧起双手，手里的火一点点长大，长到照亮了房梁。“他们教我把它压小，”她说，“我不压的时候，它就是这样。{我从没给任何人看过。”|你已经看过一次了。这个提议还算数。”}
# en: An empty duel hall at night, a crimson-haired student holding a fire that keeps growing in her cupped hands, its light up to the rafters.
scene [fdf277] = 夜里空荡荡的决斗厅，一个深红头发的学生捧着一团不断长大的火，火光一直照到房梁。
# en: Ask her to teach you
opt.left.label [431f80] = 请她教你
# en: She teaches it the way she does everything, without explaining, twice. Your fire runs on the third try and bites your wrist on the way out. "It does that," she says. "You stop apologising for it eventually."
opt.left.say.1 [47f413] = 她像做任何事一样教它：不解释，示范两遍。第三次你的火奔了出去，出去时咬了你的手腕一口。“它会这样的，”她说，“总有一天你会不再为它道歉。”
# en: Just watch her let it run
opt.right.label [ec745e] = 只看她放火奔跑
# en: You sit on the bench and watch her let it run to the rafters and back. She doesn't offer again tonight. On the way out she says, "Another time," which from Lyra is a promise.
opt.right.say.1 [b02520] = 你坐在长凳上，看她让火奔向房梁又奔回来。今晚她没再提。出门时她说“改天吧”，从莱拉嘴里出来，这就是承诺。

@event tobias_teaches_heartwood
# en: Something to Stand Under
title [d33246] = 可以站在下面的东西
# en: Tobias kneels in an empty bed at the back of the greenhouse. "Ma used to say a farm's only as good as its shelter," he says, and presses his hands into the soil. A sapling comes up between you, then a trunk, then branches overhead. "Took me a year. I'll show you in an evening, if you like."
text [c7446d] = 托比亚斯跪在温室最里面一块空苗床前。“我妈常说，一个农场好不好，要看它的遮蔽，”他说着，把手按进土里。一棵树苗在你们之间冒了出来，然后是树干，然后枝条撑在头顶。“我花了一年。你要愿意，我一个晚上教会你。”
# en: A greenhouse at dusk, a broad young man kneeling over bare soil as a sapling shoots up into a sheltering tree between two students.
scene [9c4be4] = 黄昏的温室，一个壮实的年轻人跪在光秃秃的泥土上，一株树苗在两个学生之间蹿成一棵遮蔽的树。
# en: Kneel down beside him
opt.left.label [9f3a4e] = 跪在他旁边
# en: You kneel in the cold soil until your knees ache and your back complains. Near midnight a little tree stands up out of your bed, wobbling, and spreads one branch over you. Tobias laughs from the belly and apologises for the mud.
opt.left.say.1 [9dba49] = 你跪在冰冷的泥土里，直到膝盖酸痛、腰也抗议。快到午夜时，一棵小树摇摇晃晃地从你的苗床里站了起来，在你头顶撑开一根枝。托比亚斯从肚子里笑出来，又为满地的泥道了歉。
# en: Sit under his tree instead
opt.right.label [0c9cbd] = 改坐在他的树下
# en: You sit under his tree and he tells you a long story about a goat. It is very peaceful. "Another evening, then," he says, and means it.
opt.right.say.1 [bca719] = 你坐在他的树下，他给你讲了一个关于山羊的长故事。非常安宁。“那就改个晚上，”他说，是真心的。

@event seraphine_teaches_omen
# en: Say It So It Lands
title [60f6f8] = 说出来，让它应验
# en: Seraphine stops halfway through a sentence and looks at the candle across the observatory. "That will go out," she says, quite clearly, "when I've finished the next word." It does. "Saying it is the spell. Seeing it is just… I can teach you the saying part."
text [918803] = 瑟拉芬话说到一半停下，看着观星台另一头的蜡烛。“说完下一个词，”她清清楚楚地说，“它就会灭。”它灭了。“说出来就是咒语。看见只是……说出来那部分，我可以教你。”
# en: The observatory at night, a pale student with distant eyes speaking softly while a candle across the room gutters out exactly as she finishes.
scene [6a8ae6] = 夜里的观星台，一个眼神飘远的苍白学生轻声说话，房间另一头的蜡烛恰好在她说完时熄灭。
# en: Learn to say it out loud
opt.left.label [998886] = 学着把它说出来
# en: It takes the whole night, and it's unsettling to hear your own voice go flat and certain. Near dawn you foretell a dropped spoon and the spoon drops. Seraphine smiles at something next week.
opt.left.say.1 [73a48a] = 学了一整夜，听自己的声音变得平板而笃定，让人发毛。快天亮时你预言一把勺子会掉，勺子就掉了。瑟拉芬对着下周的某件事笑了。
# en: Ask what she sees for you
opt.right.label [49945e] = 问她看见了你的什么
# en: "Quiet," she says. "Yours is always quiet." She doesn't teach you tonight. She says you'll ask again, and you know she's right, which is the strange part.
opt.right.say.1 [236cfa] = “安静，”她说，“你的总是很安静。”今晚她没有教你。她说你会再来问的，你知道她说得对，这才是奇怪的地方。

@event corvin_teaches_sleight
# en: Watch the Other Hand
title [baef32] = 看另一只手
# en: At the Gilded Newt, Corvin rolls a coin across his knuckles, and then it's in your pocket, and then it's back in his. "Grandfather's trick," he says. "I'd teach it to a saint, if the saint promised to only use it on people who deserve it." The jokes stop. "Do you promise?"
text [39419c] = 在镀金蝾螈酒馆，科尔文让一枚硬币在指节间滚动，然后它到了你口袋里，又回到了他的口袋。“我爷爷的把戏，”他说，“我愿意教给一个圣人，只要圣人保证只用在活该的人身上。”玩笑停了。“你保证吗？”
# en: A corner table at a tavern in the evening, a grinning student holding up a coin that is clearly not where it was a moment ago.
scene [123700] = 傍晚酒馆角落的一张桌子，一个咧嘴笑的学生举起一枚硬币，它显然已经不在刚才的位置了。
# en: Promise, and learn it
opt.left.label [716332] = 保证，然后学
# en: You promise. He teaches you over three drinks you don't pay for, and by the last one you lift his coin without him feeling it. He looks at you for a long moment. "Don't make me sorry," he says, quietly.
opt.left.say.1 [74d1d6] = 你保证了。他用三杯你没付钱的酒的工夫教会了你，到最后一杯时，你摸走他的硬币，他毫无察觉。他盯着你看了很久。“别让我后悔，”他轻声说。
# en: "Not that one, Corvin."
opt.right.label [d8caaa] = “这个就算了，科尔文。”
# en: "Saint," he says, fondly, and the coin goes back in his own pocket. He buys the next round anyway. You suspect he's relieved.
opt.right.say.1 [2407ea] = “圣人，”他说，语气亲昵，硬币回到了他自己的口袋。他还是请了下一轮。你怀疑他松了口气。

@event mir_teaches_contraption
# en: It Probably Works
title [771dd5] = 大概能用
# en: Mir sweeps a bench clear with one arm. "Watch!" A kettle, a mantel clock and a spoon jump together into a whirring thing that pours tea, mostly into the cup. "No plans, no drawings, just ask the bits what they want to be! It's my own. It probably won't explode. Want it?"
text [453e90] = 米尔一挥胳膊把工作台清空。“看！”一把水壶、一座壁钟和一把勺子跳到一起，变成一个嗡嗡作响、会倒茶的东西，茶大部分倒进了杯子。“不用图纸，不用设计，只要问零件想变成什么！这是我自己的。大概不会爆炸。想要吗？”
# en: A cluttered workshop, an artificer flinging together a whirring machine from a kettle, a clock and a spoon while another student ducks.
scene [1876f4] = 一间杂乱的工坊，一位机械师用水壶、时钟和勺子拼出一台呼呼转的机器，另一个学生赶紧低头躲。
# en: Yes, show me how
opt.left.label [e7175f] = 要，教我怎么做
# en: Your first one is a teapot that walks and the second one sparks and singes your eyebrows. The third pours tea. Mir writes your name in a notebook, which you understand is the highest honour Mir has.
opt.left.say.1 [cf4b5e] = 你的第一台是一只会走路的茶壶，第二台冒火花燎了你的眉毛。第三台会倒茶。米尔把你的名字写进了笔记本，你明白这是米尔能给的最高荣誉。
# en: Help them clean up instead
opt.right.label [d457a0] = 改帮米尔收拾
# en: You help sort the bits back into their drawers while Mir explains every one. "Next time," Mir says, "you're building. Probably."
opt.right.say.1 [e1e41b] = 你帮着把零件分回抽屉，米尔把每一样都讲给你听。“下回，”米尔说，“你来造。大概吧。”

@event kael_teaches_hoarfrost
# en: Cold Hands
title [a4a2d1] = 冰冷的手
# en: Kael holds his hand over a brazier in the courtyard, and the coals grey over with frost until the fire gives up. "Where I come from, everyone learns this before they learn to read," he says. A pause. "It's for putting fires out. Mostly. I could teach you, if you wanted it."
text [aec993] = 凯尔把手悬在庭院的火盆上，炭火蒙上一层白霜，直到火认了输。“在我们那儿，人人识字之前就先学这个，”他说。停顿。“是用来灭火的。大多数时候。你要是想要，我可以教你。”
# en: A frosty courtyard at night, a quiet student holding a hand over a brazier as rime creeps across its coals and the fire dies down.
scene [439e75] = 结霜的夜间庭院，一个安静的学生把手悬在火盆上，白霜爬过炭块，火渐渐熄了。
# en: "I want it."
opt.left.label [b2d92f] = “我想要。”
# en: He seems startled that you said it out loud. He takes your hands to show you, and his are as cold as ever. By the end your fingers ache and the brazier is frosted grey. "Good," he says, and doesn't let go at once.
opt.left.say.1 [d39fb4] = 你把这话说出口，他似乎吃了一惊。他握住你的手示范，他的手还是那么冷。到最后你的手指发疼，火盆结了一层灰白的霜。“好，”他说，没有立刻松手。
# en: Warm his hands instead
opt.right.label [c09ca8] = 改去暖他的手
# en: You take his hands and hold them over the last of the fire. He doesn't say anything for a long time. "Another night," he says, eventually, about the spell or the hands.
opt.right.say.1 [138704] = 你握住他的手，放在最后一点火上。他很久没说话。“改个晚上吧，”他终于说——说的是咒语，还是手，你不确定。

@event nessa_teaches_candour
# en: Off the Record
title [a5d3b6] = 不予记录
# en: Nessa puts her quill down, says "off the record", and it goes still. "Here's the real trick of interviews," she says. "Ask the question they want to answer. And then this." She says a word, and you find yourself telling her the truth about your exams. "That's Candour. Want it?"
text [4579a4] = 内莎放下羽毛笔，说了句“不予记录”，笔就不动了。“采访真正的诀窍是，”她说，“问对方想回答的问题。然后是这个。”她说了一个词，你发现自己把考试的实情全告诉了她。“这就是坦言。想要吗？”
# en: A newspaper office after midnight, an editor setting down her quill which goes still, two students talking quietly over cold tea.
scene [e4fe83] = 午夜后的报社，一位编辑放下羽毛笔，笔静止不动，两个学生在凉掉的茶旁低声交谈。
# en: Learn it from her
opt.left.label [f81f8d] = 跟她学
# en: She practises on you until you've told her three embarrassing things, then lets you practise on her. She tells you one true thing, quietly, and asks you never to print it. You won't.
opt.left.say.1 [2f71f3] = 她拿你练，直到你说出三件丢脸的事，然后让你拿她练。她轻声告诉你一件真事，请你永远别登出来。你不会的。
# en: Ask it on the record
opt.right.label [66005c] = 要求“予以记录”
# en: She laughs, picks up the quill and interviews you about why you won't learn it. It runs on page four. "Another night," she says. "Off the record."
opt.right.say.1 [115745] = 她笑了，拿起羽毛笔，采访你为什么不肯学。报道登在第四版。“改个晚上吧，”她说，“不予记录。”
